  "text": "ultureInfo\n\n\\ActiveFormice\n\\ActiveFormice\n\\ActiveFormice\n\n�新 X\n�新 X\n�新 X\n\nﺗ.FAILURE\n.Fatalfure\n.Fatalfure\n\n\\ActiveFormice\n\\ActiveFormice\n\\ActiveFormice\n\\ActiveFormice\n\nWhat is the least possible total number of meals they need to prepare?\nTo solve this problem, we first need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of the numbers of people in each group. This is because we need to prepare the same number of meals for each group to ensure that each group gets the same variety of food items.\n\nThe numbers of people in each group are:\n- Athletes: 8 (per box)\n- Coaches: 4 (per box)\n- Officials: 1 (individual package)\n\nThus, we need the least common multiple of 8, 4, and 1. The LCM of 8 and 4 is 8, since 8 is a multiple of 4, and 8 is the smallest number that both 8 and 4 can divide into without leaving a remainder. Therefore, the LCM of 8, 4, and 1 is 8.\n\nThe least possible total number of meals they need to prepare is 8.",
